# Canonical author identity.
#
# The `Cranot`, `Dimitris` and `t` identities are all the same person, spread
# across machines and git configs over the life of the repo. Folding them here
# makes `git shortlog`, `git blame`, `git log --use-mailmap` and GitHub's
# contributor graph agree, without rewriting published history.
#
# Deliberately NOT remapped:
#   - amir-rezaei and holive are genuine outside contributors.
#   - prakteon-operator, stoa and stoa-automerge are automation identities.
#     They share an address with a human identity but are a different actor,
#     which is why the entries below that touch that address match on name as
#     well as email rather than on email alone.

